														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2010440">
									

<p>I agree with all this. It doesn't presently stand on its own. It's perfectly fine to <em>heavily</em> tie in with other material, but it should either be part of a larger tale sequence (that makes a whole story) or have enough material here to stand on its own.</p>
<p>No vote for now.</p>
<p>EDIT: For clarity, it's not that the crossover is bad, at all, it's that there's not enough story material here for me. That would be cool if I were reading a story made up of consecutive sections (like In His Own Image) but I'm not.</p>

